'' A '#cmdline' RESTART LEAVES NO INTERMEDIATE OBJECT. The '#cmdline' follows a statement,
'' so the header pre-scan (T75) misses it: pass one builds acme/twice into '<exe>.<id>.o',
'' the unit's own pass restarts, and the restarted pass takes the module from the cache.
'' Pass one's object was never deleted -- app.exe.80.o beside the program, eight of them
'' for a one-file program importing std and tkl (2026-10-12). 80 is the module source's
'' file id in this fixture; a fresh cache makes pass one miss, as a first build does.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_MODCACHE=build/.mct-cmdline/cache
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.mct-cmdline
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc -i tests/modules/src/cmdlinetemps/libs tests/modules/src/cmdlinetemps/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-cmdline/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: build/.mct-cmdline/app.exe
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.mct-cmdline/app.exe.80.o
'' RUN: build/.mct-cmdline/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  42
